  "kept": [
   {
    "sentenceId": 1,
    "text": "Both are making 100 grand a year where they're taking home $8,333 a month and then on top of that You have two different people, one's a spender, one's a saver.",
    "beat": "NUMBER"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 0,
    "text": "So I have a picture here of two different people and I'm just kind of curious who would you rather be?",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 2,
    "text": "So one, you are a very nice house or a car or rent.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 3,
    "text": "So you have a very expensive apartment, $5,000 a month, you have $1,600 you're paying for your car, and then you travel a lot.",
    "beat": "NUMBER"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 4,
    "text": "So you're paying $1,000 a month just to travel.",
    "beat": "NUMBER"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 5,
    "text": "So end up saving about $733 a month, or would you rather be the other person who's doing $3,500, they own a house instead of renting like the other person, they have $200 just for their car insurance since they own their car, and then also $500 for travel because they're a little bit more modest,",
    "beat": "NUMBER"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 6,
    "text": "they don't really gotta travel that much, saving $4,133 a month.",
    "beat": "NUMBER"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 7,
    "text": "Now which one are you and which one would you rather be if you're the other or not?",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 9,
    "text": "I would rather be the saver so and I am",
    "beat": "PAYOFF"
   }
